Lepton: list only codecs the VA-API driver decodes; log the decode path

ro.waydroid.hwcodecs (which video codecs the GPU decodes) is set by
WayDroid's container manager; Lepton has none, so the service either listed
every FFmpeg video decoder as "hardware" or, with
debug.ffmpeg-codec2.hwaccel.force, none of the checked ones. When the
property is empty and media.sf.hwaccel is set, query the VA-API driver once
(profiles with a VLD entry point) and use that list; log it as
LEPTON_VA_CAPS. With force, also hide the other FFmpeg video decoders
(MPEG-2/4, H.263, DivX, WMV...) unless the GPU decodes them, so FFmpeg
software decoders do not replace Android's own.

Log each decode session once (LEPTON_VA_SESSION: codec, profile, size,
decode=vaapi or software with the reason) and its frame counts when it ends
(LEPTON_VA_SESSION_END: hardware frames, software frames, failed hardware
frame downloads), so FFmpeg's internal software fallback (e.g. a profile
the GPU cannot decode) is not mistaken for hardware decoding.

